# Reads & writes

The defaults cover most of it. When you want a named view or a transactional change,
write it **inside** the resource.

A **query** is a live view — when the data changes, every page reading it updates,
no reload. Here's the ranked board, hottest first:

resource Lead do
  query :ranked, where: status == :scored, order: [desc: :score]
  query :backlog, where: status != :scored
end

A **mutation** is an all-or-nothing change, run server-side. It returns the new shape;
the page re-renders the moment it lands:

resource Lead, grant: [net: "api.crm.com"] do
  mutation :enrich do
    %{revenue: Dock.fetch(crm_url(name)).revenue, status: :enriched}
  end
end

Same idea as the rest of the format: the page isn't a snapshot of the store —
**the page is the store**. A scored lead grows its bar the instant `:enrich` commits.

One resource, many views; the source of truth stays in one place. The [[Pipeline]]
reads `:backlog`, the dashboard and [[Score chart]] read `:ranked`. Run `work why :lead`
to see who touches it.
